# Keep the content-engine source out of the deployment.
#
# The site is served from the repo root, so anything committed here is otherwise
# fetchable at https://www.jorgebernardo.tech/<path> — /generate-post.mjs,
# /CLAUDE.md and /docs/PRODUCT.md all returned 200, and robots.txt invites every
# crawler (incl. GPTBot/ClaudeBot) to index them. The repo is public, so this is
# crawl hygiene rather than secrecy, plus one layer of protection if a future
# commit ever lands something at the root before .gitignore catches it.
#
# Paths are root-anchored on purpose. Everything the live site needs must stay:
#   index.html  blog/  privacidade/  relatorios/  images/  social/  api/
#   favicon.png  apple-touch-icon.png  sitemap.xml  robots.txt  feed.xml
#   podcast.xml  podcast-cover.jpg  package.json  vercel.json
# social/ is load-bearing — post-to-instagram.mjs builds Graph API media URLs
# from ${SITE_URL}/social/<id>/*.png and fails if they are not reachable.

# Pipeline scripts (dev/VPS only — never executed by Vercel).
/*.mjs

# Repo-facing docs and instructions.
/CLAUDE.md
/README.md
/docs/
/.impeccable/

# Carousel/video source templates, rendered server-side into images.
/templates/

# CI definitions and local scratch.
/.github/
/temp/
/sim/

# Pipeline ledgers — read by the generators on the VPS, never by a browser.
/cycling-topics-bank.json
/signal-sources.json
/used-signals.json

# Report panel specs (dev-only, read by generate-report-images.mjs).
/relatorios/*/panels.mjs
/relatorios/*/instagram.md

# One-off project workspaces (dev only, never served).
/projects/

# Full-resolution photo masters. These are the SOURCE for optimize-images.mjs and stay
# in git, but nothing on the site links to them any more: index.html serves the
# responsive ladder in images/opt/ instead. Shipping them was 107 MB of deploy weight
# for files no browser requested. Root-anchored with an extension glob so images/opt/
# and the logo PNGs are untouched.
/images/*.jpg
/images/*.jpeg

# Superseded blog art. Each post generated a ~1.94 MB PNG (105 MB across the archive)
# that was only ever an og:image; posts now reference the .jpg/.webp pair beside it.
/blog/posts/images/*.png
